1.24.0: the scene - white balance, tone, graduated ND before the camera

Nine adjustments on the light before the camera stage, all
scene-linear, all identity at 0 (renders with none of them set are
byte-identical to 1.23): temp and tint (white balance in stops of
channel ratio; +1 temp a stop warmer, +1 tint a stop toward magenta),
black (the black point: crush or fog, in scene units), shadows (lift or
drop the bottom stops with a soft knee, full effect four stops under
middle gray, hue and saturation kept), highlights (the raw shoulder's
knee, 0.5..0.9 of display white; scene-linear input only, a JPEG has
no headroom), contrast (a log gamma about middle gray on luminance,
color ratios kept), and a graduated neutral-density filter - grad
(density in stops at the dark edge), gradangle (0 top, 90 right, 180
bottom, 270 left) and gradpos (the transition's center as an offset
from the frame center; it feathers over a quarter of the frame).
Order in the pipeline: white balance and the filter on the light, then
exposure, then black, shadows and contrast, then the knee at the
shoulder.

One table of the scene keys (name, range) in the core -
pj_scene_keys, pj_scene_is_key, pj_scene_set, pj_scene_get - is the
reader for every front end: --temp and friends on polajuice and
superjuice, the recipe keys, the server's query, the wasm's one SCENE
argument ("k=v,k=v"), and TEMP= and friends in super8ify. The page
has the nine in the Scene group with labels in their units, writes
them into the recipe and the CLI line, and brackets warm/cool,
shadows, contrast and grad. The recipe gains nine keys; readers from
before 1.24 ignore them with a note.

Tests: core checks each stage moves the picture the way its name
says on the test pattern (white balance on channel ratios, shadows on
the dark corner against a midtone, black both ways, contrast on the
spread, the grad from the top and from the right, the knee both ways
through the scene-linear door) and the key table's parsing, ranges and
formatting; compat round-trips all nine through a recipe file and a
JPEG, refuses an out-of-range value and checks zero is identity;
serve renders a scene query byte-identical to the CLI and refuses
temp=5; wasm checks effect, embedded recipe, identity at zero and
range; the page tests check the sliders, the recipe and the CLI line,
and Chromium a slider's re-render.

